1. Cabinet Office of Japan — "国民の祝日" (National Holidays) CSV
----------------------------------------------------------------
Source (CSV):
  https://www8.cao.go.jp/chosei/shukujitsu/syukujitsu.csv

Overview page:
  https://www8.cao.go.jp/chosei/shukujitsu/gaiyou.html

Terms of use (内閣府ホームページ利用規約):
  https://www.cao.go.jp/notice/rule.html

Index of site notices (利用案内):
  https://www.cao.go.jp/notice.html

The CSV is used as the authoritative past / confirmed holiday override data
(from 1955 onward). Redistribution and reuse must follow the Cabinet Office
website terms linked above.

2. Japanese Law Translation Database System — English holiday names
-------------------------------------------------------------------
Primary source for English display titles of the current 16 national holidays:
  Act on National Holidays (Act No. 178 of 1948), English translation
  https://www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp/en/laws/view/4846/en

Terms of Use:
  https://www.japaneselawtranslation.go.jp/en/index/terms

These English names are **reference translations**, not official texts.
The official text of Japanese law is the Japanese version only. The English
titles in this package are for display convenience and must be used in
accordance with the Japanese Law Translation Database System Terms of Use.

3. Package-authored fixed translations
--------------------------------------
Substitute Holiday / Citizens' Holiday / Public Holiday (CSV opaque label
「休日」) and some historical or one-off romanizations are package-authored
display strings, not taken from the Act translation Article 3 proper nouns.
See docs/specs/display-title-i18n.md for details.

